lbur zelinksy", "url": "https://geographyeducation.org/articles/older-articles/remembering-wilbur-zelinksy/"}, {"title": "www.scielo.org.mx", "url": "https://www.scielo.org.mx/pdf/igeo/n82/n82a15.pdf"}, {"title": "remembering wilbur zelinksy", "url": "https://geographyeducation.org/2013/10/20/remembering-wilbur-zelinksy/"}]}, "Wilbur Zelinsky earned his master's degree from the University of Wisconsin. A Sage encyclopedia entry gives the year as 1946, while the Wikipedia article doesn't give a date. Its education field lists the University of Wisconsin, Madison for the MA.\n\n- **Master's:** The Sage entry says he received a master's from the University of Wisconsin in 1946, after finishing his bachelor's at Berkeley in 1944 (He completed his baccalaureate at the University of California at Berkeley in 1944, earned a master's degree from the University of Wisconsin in 1946). Wikipedia's text names the school \"University of Madison, Wisconsin\" (his Master's degree from the University of Madison, Wisconsin), which appears to be a naming error for UW–Madison.\n- **Bachelor's and PhD:** His bachelor's was from UC Berkeley, and he returned there for his PhD, completed in 1953 (returned to Berkeley for his PhD, which he completed in 1953).\n- **Career:** He later joined Penn State's geography department in 1963 and became professor emeritus in 1987 (He joined the geography department at Pennsylvania State University in 1963, where he has remained ever since. He was department head from 1970 to 1976, assumed emeritus status in 1987). He died on May 4, 2013, at age 91 (died on May 4, 2013, at age 91)."], "durationSeconds": 6.041054708000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01C1isBzDKLiYKejmi92cZLN", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
